  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-08T15:52:41.935Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've noticed a trend with vrchat where frequently they will add some sort of update that significantly alters the game. Yet we'll just treat the announcement of it like they do any other update.\n\nTruth is a lot of players don't care enough to read the change logs.\n\nFor example recently a limiter for dynamic bones was added. yet because it was basically just talked about in the normal change logs and not much else where I had many players that I had to keep explaining to that this new system was in place and how to change/disable it. And a very similar thing happened when the safety system was implemented. even on servers that are heavily vrchat related there was plenty of panic about the fact that their Dynamic bones wasn't working anymore or people were confused about the new name tags and why they weren't seeing some features on certain colors etc\n\nI think there needs to be some sort of significant and noticeable, but short and concise announcement about the update in game for players either through a direct notification in your menu similar to like a friend request or an invite, or even a notification similar to the one you receive when you join a community Labs world where regardless of your settings it will display the same message for everyone and you have to hit go to actually load in.\n\n  And obviously the system shouldn't be enabled by default it should be up to the player if they want to enable whatever the new feature is instead of confusing players who might not have heard about the feature. and causing unnecessary panic and damage control because a lot of players now think that the game has some sort of major bug",
